      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chiltoncountyhistoricalsociety.org/Verbena/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "During yellow fever outbreaks in the late 1800s and early 1900s, affluent Montgomery residents fled to Verbena, turning it into a seasonal resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbena%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The South & North Alabama Railroad ran through Verbena in the 1860s, and the town still sits beside the CSX line that traces that historic route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        7,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
